# ADR: Preserve dependence through symbolic expressions

## Status
Accepted

## Context
Conjevture combines learned judgments with exact Boolean rules. Reusing
an uncertain proposition must preserve its identity and dependence.

## Decision
Keep scoped variable handles and immutable symbolic expressions. Evaluate
small explicit joint distributions by enumerating possible worlds.
Require a stated reason to combine disjoint groups as independent.
Keep Jev response conversion separate from the dependency-free core.

## Alternatives considered
- Combining scalar probabilities at each gate loses shared identity.
- Compiled inference adds machinery beyond the scope of version 0.1.

## Consequences
Enumeration remains inspectable and is limited to 65,536 worlds by default.
The caller supplies dependence information and selects action policies.
The initial public repository includes an MIT license and a short README
that links to the complete guide.

## Validation
All 23 runtime tests and TypeScript contracts pass after a clean install.
Both examples return the expected probabilities. Documentation links,
package contents, and staged whitespace checks pass.
